---
title: Reports
description: Balance sheet, income statement and account ledger.
---

All reports are under **Accounting** and show one period at a time: pick it with **Period**. By default you see the current year.

## Balance sheet

What you own and what you owe, with your equity. Until the year is closed, the profit or loss so far shows as **Result of the period**, so the balance sheet always adds up.

If it ever doesn't, nullish warns you: **Assets and liabilities do not balance.**

## Income statement

Your income and expenses for the period, and the resulting **Profit or loss**.

## Account ledger

Every posting on one account, with its running **Balance**. Pick the account from the list of accounts that moved during the period, or step through them one by one. Filter by number, dates or reference, and click a row to open its journal entry.

## VAT declaration

See [VAT](/en/accounting/vat/#vat-declaration).
